From 3f572f8930de784d41f5c652cdedb6c675e719db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YOUR NAME <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:54:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: Let the ADSP write its sensor registry under
 persist

The sensor PD on the Lenovo TB710FU (SM8650) writes its registry during
initialization. It opens /mnt/vendor/persist/sensors/registry/registry/DIR
for writing and later replaces files by writing fstempfile and renaming
it. hexagonrpcd is read-only, so the registry sensor never comes up and
SSC reports no sensors.

Implement fwrite, fsync, fremove, mkdir, ftrunc and frename in apps_std,
limited to paths below /mnt/vendor/persist and /persist. Writes reach the
host through new optional hexagonfs operations, which only the mapped
file type implements. Receive up to 64 KiB per message, because fwrite
carries its data inline.

The whole persist/sensors/registry directory is now mapped, because the
sensor PD also keeps sns_reg_version and parsed_file_list.csv there. The
host directory is <prefix>/sensors/persist-registry/.
